>does this mean you intend to do this again?

Sure! ...when I get in the mood again. Although I'll probably try to
change something next time to keep it interesting, like try a
"wimpier" character class, or try to tame (if possible) all of the
demon lords and ascend with them as pets, etc.  Actually the concept
of nethack being fun being the reason why we play it, is the same
thing that is behind most of the debates on the net, IMHO. For
instance, some of us have been playing for years and can easily finish
the current version with almost any character, and therefore for them
the game has gotten *boring* and no longer fun, (so they are seeking
ways to make it harder, like limiting certain features, polypiling
being the main one). However, there are a lot of neophytes out there
who haven't made it anywhere near the Medusa level, and so they think
the game is more than hard enough as it is, and with any "loopholes"
removed, the game would become too hard and be *irritating* and,
again, no longer fun. Since as the years go by, the span of playing
abilities within any game increases, we should try to make nethack fun
for all players, perhaps by having something like different definable
levels of difficulty (e.g. no polypiling = 2 million point bonus on
ascension or something) or else put any limitations on the game in
compile time #defines, such as #ifdef NOPOLYPILE, #ifdef
PROMPTBEFOREPOOLS, etc. And the more people that think nethack is fun,
the more people will want to play it. (Is that the goal?)

